    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d6">

                <pb facs="pm_d6-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d6-1"/>

                <head>PM–6. Telegram from the Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Panama<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d6-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-08-19T20:14:00-04:00">August 19, 1958,
                            8:14 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. Verbatim Text.</p>
                <p>Deliver soonest following telegraphic message from the President to President de
                    la Guardia.</p>
                <p>“August 19, 1958. I thank your Excellency for the kind message forwarded to me by
                    the Department of State after its delivery to Governor Herter by Ambassador Arias on August 5, 1958.</p>
                <pb facs="0977" n="889" type="typeset" xml:id="pg889"/>
                <p>I assure you that my Government appreciates your comments on the implementation
                    of the recently signed Act concerning employment and wage practices in the Canal
                    Zone, and they will be kept in mind while preparing the regulations under which
                    the Act will operate. It is the intention of my Government that the
                    interpretation and application of the Act will be one more step by which we
                    strengthen the ties of friendship which already unite our countries. Dwight D.
                    Eisenhower”</p>
                <p>No public release this message planed here. In view Department’s decision not to
                    release text de la Guardia message delivered Department August 5 believe
                    decision should be left to GOP whether release
                    this message. If GOP decides release, please
                    advise 2 hours in advance release time.<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d6-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d6-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d6-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 711.11-EI/8–1958. Official Use Only;
                    Priority.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d6-f2" n="2" xml:id="pm_d6-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 144 from Panama City, August 21, Amb. Harrington informed the Department of State that President de la
                    Guardia was pleased to receive President Eisenhower’s message and planned to
                    release all but the first paragraph of it to the press on August 22.
                    (711.11-EI/8–2158)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
